Project Summary (SRS) — Titanic Data Cleaning Script
What it does:
This Python script takes the raw Titanic passenger CSV file, cleans up messy and missing data, creates a few useful new columns for analysis, and saves the cleaned version to a new CSV file.
Key Steps (Requirements):
Load the file: Reads the raw Titanic-Dataset.csv file using pandas.
Clean text & duplicates: Removes duplicate rows and trims extra spaces from text columns.
Extract Titles: Pulls titles (like Mr, Mrs, Miss) out of the Name column and groups rare titles into simple labels (Royal, Officer, Other).
Fill missing values:
Embarked: Fills blank values with the most common port (S).
Age: Fills blank ages using the average (median) age of passengers with the same gender and ticket class.
Deck: Takes the first letter of Cabin as the deck, and labels missing ones as "Unknown".
Create new features:
FamilySize: Total family members aboard (SibSp + Parch + 1).
IsAlone: 1 if traveling alone, 0 if with family.
Sex_encoded: Converts male to 0 and female to 1.
Format & Save: Sets category data types for cleaner analysis, saves the final table to Titanic-Dataset-Cleaned.csv, and prints a quick check of missing values and row/column counts.
One small note:
In the function definition, the default file path is missing the C (":\\Users..."), though it works fine when run directly because __main__ passes the full C:\Users... path.
